Z||000000||RRobinson||01-11-2001||06:51 PM||||Hi, everybody!<BR>   I am new to the forum- what a fantastic resource for us Fiero owners. My name is Ryan Robinson and I am from Calgary, Alberta. I got hooked on the cute little buggers about seven years ago when I had a worn-out '86 Dodge 4x4 that I could not get rid of. In desperation, I traded it straight across for an, ahem, 'slightly' tired maroon 87 GT that looked as if it had run the Paris-Dakkar rally. Long story short, I now am lucky enough to have 3 Fieros. They are a black 87 GT 5-speed with 55,000 miles (summer driver), a red 88 GT auto with 37,000 miles, and my baby, a blue 87 GT 5-speed with 18,000 miles I picked up from a seedy car lot last year for $6000CDN (about $4000US). It's 100% original down to the old-style Eagle GT tires. (I figure it was someones baby before it was mine) I kind of like my cars original, so I have not done many modifications to any of my cars. (although there are some awesome mods on some of your cars!) Anyways, cheers!<P>Ryan<BR> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||loafer87gt||01-11-2001||07:35 PM||||Welcome to the forum! I was born in Calgary, and have since moved on to Saskatoon. There are a couple of other forum members here from Calgary (Ricecooker I think). I'm sure you'll find lots of useful stuff here, later<P>||||reg||1
